+# Global inputs (ModflowGPU T5.5a, for T5.5b)
+
+- `global.toml`: the global MODFLOW config with the chosen input files (draft for the
+  coupled global run; GPU engine). It does **not** run as is: the steady-head file has no
+  head on the 173,727 CHD cells (see below).
+- `mgv_global.toml`: the mGV config (parameters, generated routing, land-only forcing).
+- `check_inputs.jl`: reads every input through ModflowCoupling and compares the grids of
+  MODFLOW, the mGV parameters, the forcing and the routing file. The results and the
+  reasons for each file choice are in ModflowGPU's `docs/global_inputs.md`.
+- `merge_routing_tiles.py`: merges routing files of mGV-input-data's `make-routing.py`.
+
+## The global routing file
+
+mGV-input-data at `7e4418b`, HydroSHEDS v1 DEM `hyd_glo_dem_15s.tif` (from
+`hyd_glo_dem_15s.zip`, sha256 `630e92fa…5301`), in `/home/bart/data/mGV/`. The global box
+(`--bbox -180 -56 180 84`) was killed by the out-of-memory killer at 52 GB in the IHU
+upscaling step (61 GB machine, 50 GB limit), so the globe is made in two boxes split at
+-25° (Atlantic; crosses only Greenland) and merged; mGV needs routing values on every
+active cell, so the 2,841 active cells without HydroSHEDS data are added as one-cell
+basins (`--fill-domain`):
+
+```sh
+cd /home/bart/data/mGV
+uv run mGV-input-data/routing/HydroSHEDS/make-routing.py --bbox -25 -56 180 84 \
+    --dem hydrosheds/hyd_glo_dem_15s.tif --output routing/routing_5min_tile_east.nc   # 29.2 GB, 6 min
+uv run mGV-input-data/routing/HydroSHEDS/make-routing.py --bbox -180 -56 -25 84 \
+    --dem hydrosheds/hyd_glo_dem_15s.tif --output routing/routing_5min_tile_west.nc   # 21.5 GB, 3 min
+uv run <this directory>/merge_routing_tiles.py --output routing/routing_global_5min.nc \
+    --fill-domain vic_global_5min_params_lossless.nc routing/routing_5min_tile_west.nc routing/routing_5min_tile_east.nc
+```
+
+The routing grid is the parameter grid (4320 × 1680, coordinates within 5.1e-6°). The
+DEM covers 84 N to 56 S, the same extent as the parameter grid (its northernmost valid
+data at about 83.5 N).
diff --git a/examples/global/check_inputs.jl b/examples/global/check_inputs.jl
